{
    "patcher": {
        "fileversion": 1,
        "appversion": {
            "major": 9,
            "minor": 1,
            "revision": 4,
            "architecture": "x64",
            "modernui": 1
        },
        "classnamespace": "box",
        "rect": [ 85.0, 104.0, 1320.0, 600.0 ],
        "description": "_br.eq3.example.1.0 -- Created by Brian Riordan, guaguanco127@gmail.com -- https://github.com/guaguanco127/",
        "boxes": [
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-signature",
                    "linecount": 4,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 630.0, 15.0, 662.0, 60.0 ],
                    "text": "_br.eq3.example.1.0 -- Created by Brian Riordan, guaguanco127@gmail.com\nhttps://github.com/guaguanco127/\nCredits: trapezoidal (TPT) state-variable filters from V. Zavalishin, \"The Art of VA Filter Design\" (2012), and A. Simper, \"Linear Trapezoidal Integrated State Variable Filter\" (Cytomic technical paper, 2013)."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 24.0,
                    "id": "obj-2",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 15.0, 300.0, 33.0 ],
                    "text": "br.eq3"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-3",
                    "linecount": 2,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 57.0, 560.0, 33.0 ],
                    "text": "A stereo 3-band EQ in gen~: Low, Mid and High gain (-24 to 24 dB), two crossovers (Fq) and a mute (M) per band. The bands are phase-matched, so all gains at 0 dB = exactly the input."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-4",
                    "linecount": 3,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 115.0, 500.0, 47.0 ],
                    "text": "Inlets: L, R, then one per control in panel order (EQ, High, High Mute, High Crossover, Mid, Mid Mute, Low Crossover, Low, Low Mute). Hover any inlet or outlet for its range and default."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-5",
                    "linecount": 2,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 173.0, 560.0, 33.0 ],
                    "text": "Outlets: L, R. Every control glides 10 ms inside, so moves and mutes never click. Silent input costs almost no CPU."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-7",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 492.0, 560.0, 20.0 ],
                    "text": "Outputs start muted at -70 dB: turn on audio, then raise the slider slowly."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-8",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 517.0, 300.0, 20.0 ],
                    "text": "By Brian Riordan. github.com/guaguanco127"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "eq-obj-2",
                    "linecount": 2,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 220.0, 494.0, 33.0 ],
                    "text": "Pick a source and turn the bands. Click a number box and drag up or down, or type a value."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "eq-obj-3",
                    "linecount": 3,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 265.0, 302.0, 47.0 ],
                    "text": "Start: mute two bands to hear what the third one holds, then move the Fq boxes to set where it starts and ends."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "eq-obj-4",
                    "linecount": 3,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 324.0, 304.0, 47.0 ],
                    "text": "M fades its band out in 10 ms, so the mutes work as kills when playing live. EQ off = the dry input, for an A/B."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "eq-obj-5",
                    "linecount": 2,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 383.0, 474.0, 33.0 ],
                    "text": "All gains at 0 dB = exactly the input: the bands are phase-matched and add back up flat."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "eq-obj-6",
                    "linecount": 3,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 428.0, 304.0, 47.0 ],
                    "text": "The two Fq boxes sort themselves: drag the lower one past the upper one and they swap roles without a glitch."
                }
            },
            {
